#: src/android/build-rules.md:6
msgid "Build Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:8
msgid "The Android build system (Soong) supports Rust through several modules:"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:10
msgid "Module Type"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:10
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:12
msgid "`rust_binary`"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:12
msgid "Produces a Rust binary."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:13
msgid "`rust_library`"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:13
msgid "Produces a Rust library, and provides both `rlib` and `dylib` variants."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:14
msgid "`rust_ffi`"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:14
msgid ""
"Produces a Rust C library usable by `cc` modules, and provides both static "
"and shared variants."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:15
msgid "`rust_proc_macro`"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:15
msgid ""
"Produces a `proc-macro` Rust library. These are analogous to compiler "
"plugins."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:16
msgid "`rust_test`"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:16
msgid "Produces a Rust test binary that uses the standard Rust test harness."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:17
msgid "`rust_fuzz`"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:17
msgid "Produces a Rust fuzz binary leveraging `libfuzzer`."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:18
msgid "`rust_protobuf`"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:18
msgid ""
"Generates source and produces a Rust library that provides an interface for "
"a particular protobuf."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:19
msgid "`rust_bindgen`"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:19
msgid ""
"Generates source and produces a Rust library containing Rust bindings to C "
"libraries."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:21
msgid "We will look at `rust_binary` and `rust_library` next."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:25
msgid "Additional items the speaker may mention:"
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:27
msgid ""
"Cargo is not optimized for multi-language repositories, and also downloads "
"packages from the internet."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:30
msgid ""
"For compliance and performance, Android must have crates in-tree. It must "
"also interoperate with C/C++/Java code. Soong fills that gap."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:33
msgid ""
"Soong has many similarities to [Bazel](https://bazel.build/), which is the "
"open-source variant of Blaze (used in google3)."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/build-rules.md:36
msgid "Fun fact: Data from Star Trek is a Soong-type Android."
msgstr ""
